   "date": "1944-02-24",
   "from": "China Division, Office of War Information",
   "to": "U.S. Embassy, Chungking",
   "about": "Commercial messages dated from late February to March 8, 1944, report Japanese trade, transport, industrial, and insurance business.",
   "summary": "The translations trace tightening trade quotas and the restructuring of firms, alongside plans for sawmills, veneer and chemical factories, rubber and tire barter, and rice procurement. Shipping shortages affect goods ranging from hemp bags to machinery, while new wartime insurance rules prompt instructions to insure cargo, buildings, and vessels. Messages also report a destructive warehouse fire at Fort Bayard and efforts to document its losses and insurance coverage.",
